---
title: Turkey Avocado Panini
source: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/201117/turkey-avocado-panini/
---

Mash @avocado{1} and @mayonnaise{1/4%cup} together in a bowl.

Preheat the #panini press{}.

Brush the bottom of each @ciabatta rolls or large sourdough slices{2} with @olive oil{}, then place into the press oil side down.

On each sandwich place @provolone cheese{4%slices}(2 per sandwich), then half each of the @baby spinach{1%cup}, @sliced smoked turkey breast{4%oz}, @roasted red peppers{2}(sliced into strips) and avocado mixture.

Place the top of each roll onto the sandwiches. Brush with more olive oil.

Close the panini press, grilling until the rolls are toasted and crisp with grill marks, about ~{5-8%minutes}.

> This recipe makes two sandwiches; scale the ingredients as needed.
